ust me though um and  then there was a really large target of  drea because we knew a lot of her  advantages and i was trying to tell  people about the paint on her arm and  like there's something else going on  here we don't know about and so i saw it  as like kind of one of my best case  scenarios of being able to squeak by one  more time by being with people that i  had built built social bonds with as  well of like a pretty big target that we  could get out  so when you go into this challenge  unfortunately it's the one you don't win  did you think your time was up but or  were you hopeful it sounds like you were  hopeful yeah i mean i'm always going to  be hopeful because i also i love  survivor i know survivor even when it  looks like there's zero hope like  crazier things have happened and so  it sucked i mean and i look back and  it's like  it's almost better knowing that i wasn't  even gonna come in second to winning  that challenge like i was just gonna  have to rely on hopefully  strategizing and you know it didn't work  out but can't win them all i had to give  jonathan a chance you know  i'm kidding  yeah exactly yeah you got to spread the  love that was your gift to jonathan and  everybody  so when you walked into that tribal  council or rather before you went to  tribal council what was the intended  plan and did you feel confident that  the group  was going to be able to pull it off  yeah i going into tribal of course i am  terrified because paranoia and i was  a target at every single tribal i had  been to but i did have a lot of  confidence and i fully was believing  that we were going to go into tribal  drea was going to get blindsided i would  probably have a vote thrown my way from  her  and  i was going to get by and hopefully gain  footing in the game and i really do  believe that if some circumstances were  slightly shifted for example if romeo  got voted out instead of rocks or if we  had gone to tribal first i really do  think that drea would have been the  target and i would still be in the game  and when everybody walked into the  tribal council there was shock across  everyone's face seeing that roxborough  was sitting there so who did you  originally think was going to be sitting  there and then what were you thinking  when you saw that it was roxroy well  none of us really gave much thought to  the other tribal council of like oh  what's gonna happen how's that gonna  impact our vote because we were all like  a hundred percent sure it was romeo like  even people watching i'm like it looks  like it's romeo that's how we felt in  the game too so it was just more so  shocking of like  what happened to where it was brought  like it didn't necessarily make sense to  us  at the time and that's where you know  things started to  go south for me  yeah i feel like when jeff splits the  tribe into two tribes and he talks about  information being really important and  seeing that juror i think that this is  an example of how seeing who the new  juror is really affects the game  yeah and i think that there was a lot  that affected the game last night and i  think that you were able to really be  present and be part of what i think will  be one of the most memorable tribal  councils in a while i think that  the  issues that were talked about and the  points of view that were talked about  were so illuminating so what did you get  out of being able to experience that  firsthand yeah  i kind of assumed coming into the season  due to the new diversity initiatives  that a topic surrounding race would come  up i just honestly had no idea i would  be part of that conversation  because i didn't feel like i had  anything to offer to that conversation  but what i actually have learned looking  back is  one of the most important things i can  do is allow that conversation to be had  and give space and not try to invalidate  because i don't fully understand and so  even while i was sitting in that tribal  and i knew when jerry was going to play  her idol i was going home like that was  it  and i still was able to have so much  peace because for me me going home is  just my survivor dream coming to an end  which is really hard for me to like wrap  my head around because i'm a super fan i  wanted this for six years but i knew  even in that moment if drea or marianne  were to go home that would be a lot more  meaningful deeper and hurtful for them  so i actually had peace i was just  owning and i was going to kind of step  out of the way you know i was kind of  creating chaos and being messy all  season but i didn't i didn't want to do  that i felt like it would be  inappropriate and disrespectful for the  moment that was happening and so i think  hopefully something people can take away  is even if you don't understand or  you're not actively part of that  conversation it can be really powerful  to just sit back allow that to happen  and to listen  mm-hmm  and so i what what i thought was  interesting is you noted that it was  really hard to switch back into game  mode after that conversation and i think  a lot of viewers don't realize that the  players actually have a lot of power in  tribal council in terms of dictating  when they're ready to vote so can you  share more about the decision to not go  into the private voting area as usual  and do you think that there's more that  you could have done to plead your case  um  yes well for example like i did ask jeff  if we could just not have a tribal  because he was making it very clear like  this is your tribal decide and so i  asked like can we just not vote then  like it just  i'm not saying like never vote but maybe  give us more time or vote in the morning  or just let me slide by but it did just  feel like  it needed more especially like i'm a  therapist and no one knew i was a  therapist in that situation but i saw  people being very vulnerable and  sensitive and it for me especially it  just felt so wrong to oh let's go  strai