ags and i was dumping  out my water to go search for immunity  idols none of which were true but  at that point like the only thing i  could rely on was uh immunities  it's so weird how rumors like that can  really take take a life of their own in  survivor and this is where the  perception and everything is so  important so when you look back is there  anything in your game that you think you  could have done differently  oh yes yes yes yes like since i didn't  win clearly there are things i should  have done differently um i think for me  it goes all the way back to that very  first challenge for the flint when the  amulet was part of that challenge and it  was between me or drea we were both  gonna run  and she wanted to do the shorter  distance and i wanted to do the shorter  distance because i just wanted to and so  i lied to her and i told her oh the  second leg is shorter  like and that's karma for me because  like if i would have gotten that amulet  and i would have connected with hai and  lindsey i think it would have been a  totally different game um but then i  think another thing early on in the game  that would have set me up better was  reassuring my alliance members of zack  and swafi of like hey i'm lying to other  people when i talk to them like you guys  are my alliance that really hurt my game  so there's so many things i would i  would do differently i feel like i  played 10 of my potential in survivor  because i just i never had people to  play with or work with  i think that that self-reflection is so  important and now as you look back  because i know you're a huge survivor  fan what did the experience teach you  about yourself overall  i'd say one of the biggest things and  this is a big part of my journey on the  island too and so  it never got shown but you know i'm a  therapist for women with eating  disorders and i've had my own struggles  and so i came into survivor  very much wanting to gain a deeper  appreciation for like what what can my  body do what is what is it capable of  because like back home really all that  matters to a young woman is like how  does it look in the mirror but on  survivor you don't get hair makeup stuff  you don't even have mirrors so i wanted  to appreciate my body for what it was  capable of and like that's why in my  little exit thing i was like i can do so  much more than i thought and so i really  have gained a lot deeper appreciation  for my body and what it can do like  that's a message that i want other  people to be able to do in their own  life of like let's think of our bodies  outside of just the way it looks in a  mirror  i think that there's so much to win  besides the actual win and i think that  with you you were determined you were  scrappy and you were fun to watch so  honestly thank you for going out there  and playing as you and thank you for  chatting today and honestly tori i wish  you all of the best thank you so nice to  meet you  you

